<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mungo Park</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1771–1806</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mungo Park was a Scottish surgeon and explorer who made two journeys into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a> in search of the course of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>. On the first, from 1795 to 1797, he travelled up the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-gambia">Gambia</a> through Wuli and reached the Niger at Segou. His second expedition ended in 1806 when he drowned in the rapids at Bussa while under attack.</p></div>
